IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 7 -- Functions and powers conferred by Acts (ss 23 to 30).
-- Section 24B(5) and (6)(c) fix times and are in qld-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Where the section says a thing "may" be done, the rule answers JUST TRUE when its condition holds and NOTHING otherwise (a grant limited in its own wording).
-- Where the section says a thing is "not affected" or "not invalid" merely because of a stated reason, the rule answers JUST FALSE for that reason.

§ `Part 7 -- Functions and powers conferred by Acts`

§§ `s 23 -- Performance of statutory functions etc.`

-- src:409 | (1) If an Act confers a function or power on a person or body, the function may be performed, or the power may be exercised, as occasion requires.
@ref s 23(1) (src:409-409)
GIVEN `an Act confers a function or power on a person or body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the function may be performed, or the power may be exercised, as occasion requires (s 23(1))` IS
    IF `an Act confers a function or power on a person or body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:410 | (2) If an Act confers a function or power on a specified officer or the holder of a specified office, the function may be performed, or the power may be exercised, by the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned.
@ref s 23(2) (src:410-410)
GIVEN `an Act confers a function or power on a specified officer or the holder of a specified office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may perform the function or exercise the power (s 23(2))` IS
    IF `an Act confers a function or power on a specified officer or the holder of a specified office` AND `the person is the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:411 | (3) If an Act confers a function or power on a body (whether or not incorporated), the performance of the function, or the exercise of the power, is not affected merely because of vacancies in the membership of the body.
@ref s 23(3) (src:411-411)
GIVEN `an Act confers a function or power on a body (whether or not incorporated)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are vacancies in the membership of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the performance of the function or the exercise of the power is affected merely because of vacancies in the membership of the body (s 23(3))` IS
    IF `an Act confers a function or power on a body (whether or not incorporated)` AND `there are vacancies in the membership of the body` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:413 | (1) If a provision of an Act, whether expressly or by implication, confers a power (the first power) on an entity to authorise or require another entity to exercise a power (the second power), then, if the first power is exercised, the provision is taken to confer the second power on the other entity.
@ref s 23A(1) (src:413-413)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act, whether expressly or by implication, confers a power (the first power) on an entity to authorise or require another entity to exercise a power (the second power)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first power is exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is taken to confer the second power on the other entity (s 23A(1))` IS
    IF `a provision of an Act, whether expressly or by implication, confers a power (the first power) on an entity to authorise or require another entity to exercise a power (the second power)` AND `the first power is exercised`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:414 | (2) In this section—
-- src:415 | power includes doing an act or making a decision for the purpose of performing a function.
@ref s 23A(2) (src:414-415)
GIVEN `it is doing an act or making a decision for the purpose of performing a function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a power in s 23A (s 23A(2), definition power)` IS
    IF `it is doing an act or making a decision for the purpose of performing a function` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 24AA and s 24A -- amending or repealing, appointing by name or office`

-- src:418 | If an Act authorises or requires the making of an instrument or decision—
-- src:419 | (a) the power includes power to amend or repeal the instrument or decision; and
@ref s 24AA(a) (src:418-419)
GIVEN `an Act authorises or requires the making of an instrument or decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power includes power to amend or repeal the instrument or decision (s 24AA(a))` IS
    IF `an Act authorises or requires the making of an instrument or decision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:420 | (b) the power to amend or repeal the instrument or decision is exercisable in the same way, and subject to the same conditions, as the power to make the instrument or decision.
@ref s 24AA(b) (src:420-420)
GIVEN `an Act authorises or requires the making of an instrument or decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power to amend or repeal is exercisable in the same way, and subject to the same conditions, as the power to make (s 24AA(b))` IS
    IF `an Act authorises or requires the making of an instrument or decision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Way of making an appointment` IS ONE OF
    `by appointing a person or body by name`
    `by appointing a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office, by reference to the title of the office concerned`
    `in another way`

-- src:422 | (1) If an Act authorises or requires a person or body—
-- src:423 | (a) to appoint a person to an office; or
-- src:424 | (b) to appoint a person or body to exercise a power; or
-- src:425 | (c) to appoint a person or body to do another thing;
-- src:426 | the person or body may make the appointment by—
-- src:427 | (d) appointing a person or body by name; or
-- src:428 | (e) appointing a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office, by reference to the title of the office concerned.
@ref s 24A(1) (src:422-428)
GIVEN `an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office, to appoint a person or body to exercise a power, or to appoint a person or body to do another thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `Way of making an appointment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person or body may make the appointment in the way (s 24A(1))` IS
    IF NOT `an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office, to appoint a person or body to exercise a power, or to appoint a person or body to do another thing`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER way
        WHEN `in another way` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:429 | (2) An appointment of a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office, is taken to be the appointment of the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned.
@ref s 24A(2) (src:429-429)
GIVEN `the appointment is of a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment is taken to be the appointment of the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned (s 24A(2))` IS
    IF `the appointment is of a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 24B -- Acting appointments`

-- src:431 | (1) If an Act authorises a person or body to appoint a person to act in an office, the person or body may, in accordance with the Act, appoint—
-- src:432 | (a) a person by name; or
-- src:433 | (b) a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office, by reference to the title of the office concerned;
-- src:434 | to act in the office.
@ref s 24B(1) (src:431-434)
GIVEN `an Act authorises a person or body to appoint a person to act in an office` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `Way of making an appointment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person or body may, in accordance with the Act, appoint to act in the office in the way (s 24B(1))` IS
    IF NOT `an Act authorises a person or body to appoint a person to act in an office`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER way
        WHEN `in another way` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:435 | (2) The appointment may be expressed to have effect only in the circumstances specified in the instrument of appointment.
@ref s 24B(2) (src:435-435)
GIVEN `the appointment is an appointment to act in an office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment may be expressed to have effect only in the circumstances specified in the instrument of appointment (s 24B(2))` IS
    IF `the appointment is an appointment to act in an office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Thing the appointer may do` IS ONE OF
    `determine the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances`
    `end the appointment at any time`
    `anything else`

-- src:436 | (3) The appointer may—
-- src:437 | (a) determine the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances; and
-- src:438 | (b) end the appointment at any time.
@ref s 24B(3) (src:436-438)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing the appointer may do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointer may do the thing (s 24B(3))` IS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:439 | (3A) If the appointer is a body, the appointment may be made or ended by a resolution of the body.
@ref s 24B(3A) (src:439-439)
GIVEN `the appointer is a body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment may be made or ended by a resolution of the body (s 24B(3A))` IS
    IF `the appointer is a body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): the appointment, or the ending, must be in, or evidenced by, writing signed by the appointer or, if the appointer is a body, by a person authorised by the body.
-- The rule answers whether the requirement is met; the text does not say what follows if it is not.
-- src:440 | (4) The appointment, or the ending of the appointment under subsection (3)(b), must be in, or evidenced by, writing, signed by the appointer or, if the appointer is a body, by a person authorised by the body for the purpose.
@ref s 24B(4) (src:440-440)
GIVEN `the appointment, or the ending of the appointment, is in or evidenced by writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointer is a body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is signed by the appointer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is signed by a person authorised by the body for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requirement for writing and signature is met (s 24B(4))` IS
    JUST (   `the appointment, or the ending of the appointment, is in or evidenced by writing`
         AND (IF `the appointer is a body` THEN `the writing is signed by a person authorised by the body for the purpose` ELSE `the writing is signed by the appointer`))

-- (6): the appointee acting otherwise than because of a vacancy may, subject to (2), continue to act after the office becomes vacant until the first of (a), (b), (c).
-- src:444 | (6) If the appointee is acting in the office otherwise than because of a vacancy in the office and the office becomes vacant, then, subject to subsection (2), the appointee may continue to act until—
-- src:445 | (a) the appointer otherwise directs; or
-- src:446 | (b) the vacancy ends; or
-- src:447 | (c) the end of a year from the day of the vacancy;
-- src:448 | whichever happens first.
@ref s 24B(6) (src:444-448)
GIVEN `the appointee is acting in the office otherwise than because of a vacancy in the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office has become vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointer has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a year from the day of the vacancy has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointee may continue to act (s 24B(6))` IS
    IF `the appointee is acting in the office otherwise than because of a vacancy in the office` AND `the office has become vacant`
    THEN JUST (NOT (`the appointer has otherwise directed` OR `the vacancy has ended` OR `a year from the day of the vacancy has ended`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:449 | (6A) Subsection (6)(c) does not prevent a further appointment of the appointee to act for a period ending later than a year from the day of the vacancy.
@ref s 24B(6A) (src:449-449)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 24B(6)(c) prevents a further appointment of the appointee to act for a period ending later than a year from the day of the vacancy (s 24B(6A))` IS FALSE

-- src:450 | (7) The appointment ends if the appointee resigns by writing signed and delivered to the appointer.
@ref s 24B(7) (src:450-450)
GIVEN `the appointee resigns by writing signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is delivered to the appointer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment ends (s 24B(7))` IS
    IF `the appointee resigns by writing signed` AND `the writing is delivered to the appointer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:451 | (7A) If the vacancy in the office in which a person is acting ends, the person’s appointment to act in the office because of the vacancy also ends.
@ref s 24B(7A) (src:451-451)
GIVEN `the person is acting in the office because of the vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy in the office ends` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person's appointment to act because of the vacancy ends (s 24B(7A))` IS
    IF `the person is acting in the office because of the vacancy` AND `the vacancy in the office ends` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:452 | (7B) If the holder of the office in which a person is acting resumes the office, the person’s appointment to act in the office because of the absence of the holder of the office ends.
@ref s 24B(7B) (src:452-452)
GIVEN `the person is acting in the office because of the absence of the holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder of the office resumes the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person's appointment to act because of the absence of the holder ends (s 24B(7B))` IS
    IF `the person is acting in the office because of the absence of the holder` AND `the holder of the office resumes the office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:453 | (7C) Subsections (7A) and (7B) apply even if a contrary intention appears in the instrument of, or evidencing the, appointment to act.
@ref s 24B(7C) (src:453-453)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears in the instrument of, or evidencing the, appointment to act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsections (7A) and (7B) apply (s 24B(7C))` IS JUST TRUE

-- src:454 | (7D) A person’s substantive appointment to an office does not end merely because the person acts in another office.
@ref s 24B(7D) (src:454-454)
GIVEN `the person acts in another office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person's substantive appointment to an office ends merely because the person acts in another office (s 24B(7D))` IS
    IF `the person acts in another office` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:455 | (7E) To avoid any doubt, it is declared that subsections (7A) to (7D) do not change the law of Queensland.
@ref s 24B(7E) (src:455-455)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsections (7A) to (7D) change the law of Queensland (s 24B(7E))` IS FALSE

-- src:456 | (8) While the appointee is acting in the office—
-- src:457 | (a) the appointee has all the functions and powers of the holder of the office; and
-- src:458 | (b) laws apply to the appointee, and to other persons in relationship to the appointee, as if the appointee were the holder of the office.
@ref s 24B(8) (src:456-458)
GIVEN `the appointee is acting in the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointee has all the functions and powers of the holder of the office, and laws apply as if the appointee were the holder (s 24B(8))` IS
    IF `the appointee is acting in the office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Reason relied on for treating a thing done as invalid` IS ONE OF
    `the occasion for the appointment had not arisen`
    `the appointment had ended`
    `the occasion for the person to act had not arisen or had ended`
    `another reason`

-- src:459 | (9) Anything done by or in relation to a person purporting to act in the office is not invalid merely because—
-- src:460 | (a) the occasion for the appointment had not arisen; or
-- src:461 | (b) the appointment had ended; or
-- src:462 | (c) the occasion for the person to act had not arisen or had ended.
@ref s 24B(9) (src:459-462)
GIVEN `the thing is done by or in relation to a person purporting to act in the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A `Reason relied on for treating a thing done as invalid`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing done is invalid merely because of the reason (s 24B(9))` IS
    IF NOT `the thing is done by or in relation to a person purporting to act in the office`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER reason
        WHEN `another reason` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:463 | (10) If the Act authorises the appointer to appoint a person to act during a vacancy in the office, an appointment to act in the office may be made by the appointer whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office.
@ref s 24B(10) (src:463-463)
GIVEN `the Act authorises the appointer to appoint a person to act during a vacancy in the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appointment has previously been made to the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appointment to act in the office may be made by the appointer (s 24B(10))` IS
    IF `the Act authorises the appointer to appoint a person to act during a vacancy in the office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:464 | (11) If—
-- src:465 | (a) the appointer is a specified officer or the holder of a specified office; and
-- src:466 | (b) the person who was the specified officer or holder of the specified office when the appointment was made ceases to be the officer or holder of the office;
-- src:467 | then—
-- src:468 | (c) the appointment continues in force; and
-- src:469 | (d) the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned is taken to be the appointer for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 24B(11) (src:464-469)
GIVEN `the appointer is a specified officer or the holder of a specified office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who was the specified officer or holder when the appointment was made ceases to be the officer or holder of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment continues in force and the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office is taken to be the appointer (s 24B(11))` IS
    IF `the appointer is a specified officer or the holder of a specified office` AND `the person who was the specified officer or holder when the appointment was made ceases to be the officer or holder of the office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:470 | (12) If—
-- src:471 | (a) the appointer is a body; and
-- src:472 | (b) there is a change in the membership of the body;
-- src:473 | then—
-- src:474 | (c) the appointment continues in force; and
-- src:475 | (d) the body as constituted for the time being is taken to be the appointer for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 24B(12) (src:470-475)
GIVEN `the appointer is a body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a change in the membership of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment continues in force and the body as constituted for the time being is taken to be the appointer (s 24B(12))` IS
    IF `the appointer is a body` AND `there is a change in the membership of the body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:476 | (13) Writing purporting to be, or to contain, an appointment, or the ending of an appointment under subsection (3)(b), is evidence of the appointment or the ending of the appointment.
@ref s 24B(13) (src:476-476)
GIVEN `the writing purports to be, or to contain, an appointment, or the ending of an appointment under subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the writing is evidence of the appointment or the ending of the appointment (s 24B(13))` IS
    IF `the writing purports to be, or to contain, an appointment, or the ending of an appointment under subsection (3)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:477 | (14) A certificate signed by the appointer (or, if the appointer is a body, by a person authorised by the body for the purpose) stating anything in relation to an appointment is evidence of the thing.
@ref s 24B(14) (src:477-477)
GIVEN `the certificate is signed by the appointer (or, if the appointer is a body, by a person authorised by the body for the purpose)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states something in relation to an appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is evidence of the thing it states (s 24B(14))` IS
    IF `the certificate is signed by the appointer (or, if the appointer is a body, by a person authorised by the body for the purpose)` AND `the certificate states something in relation to an appointment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (15): a document purporting to be a certificate is taken to be the certificate, and to have been properly given, unless the contrary is established.
-- FORK once the contrary is established: NOTHING (the presumption is displaced and the subsection no longer answers) || JUST FALSE (the document is not the certificate)
-- src:478 | (15) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in subsection (14) is taken to be the certificate, and to have been properly given, unless the contrary is established.
@ref s 24B(15) (src:478-478)
GIVEN `the document purports to be a certificate mentioned in subsection (14)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document is taken to be the certificate, and to have been properly given (s 24B(15))` IS
    IF `the document purports to be a certificate mentioned in subsection (14)` AND (NOT `the contrary is established`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 24C -- Acting person nominated by Act etc.`

-- src:480 | (1) This section applies if an Act provides that a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office, (the nominated person) acts as another specified officer or in another specified office on a specified occasion.
@ref s 24C(1) (src:480-480)
GIVEN `an Act provides that a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office, (the nominated person) acts as another specified officer or in another specified office on a specified occasion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 24C applies (s 24C(1))` IS
    IF `an Act provides that a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office, (the nominated person) acts as another specified officer or in another specified office on a specified occasion` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:481 | (2) While the nominated person is acting as the other officer or in the other office—
-- src:482 | (a) the nominated person has all the functions and powers of the officer or holder of the office; and
-- src:483 | (b) laws apply to the nominated person, and to other persons in relationship to the nominated person, as if the nominated person were the officer or holder of the office.
@ref s 24C(2) (src:481-483)
GIVEN `s 24C applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominated person is acting as the other officer or in the other office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nominated person has all the functions and powers, and laws apply as if the nominated person were the officer or holder of the office (s 24C(2))` IS
    IF `s 24C applies` AND `the nominated person is acting as the other officer or in the other office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:484 | (3) Anything done by or in relation to the nominated person while the nominated person is purporting to act as the other officer or in the other office is not invalid merely because the occasion for the nominated person to act had not happened or had ceased.
@ref s 24C(3) (src:484-484)
GIVEN `s 24C applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominated person is purporting to act as the other officer or in the other office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occasion for the nominated person to act had not happened or had ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing done is invalid merely because the occasion for the nominated person to act had not happened or had ceased (s 24C(3))` IS
    IF `s 24C applies` AND `the nominated person is purporting to act as the other officer or in the other office` AND `the occasion for the nominated person to act had not happened or had ceased`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 25 -- Powers of appointment imply certain incidental powers`

DECLARE `Power included in a power of appointment` IS ONE OF
    `power to remove or suspend, at any time, a person appointed to the office`
    `power to appoint another person to act in the office if a person appointed to the office is removed or suspended`
    `power to reinstate or reappoint a person removed or suspended`
    `power to appoint a person to act in the office if it is vacant (whether or not the office has ever been filled)`
    `power to appoint a person to act in the office if the person appointed to the office is absent or is unable to discharge the functions of the office (whether because of illness or otherwise)`
    `any other power`

-- src:486 | (1) If an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office—
-- src:487 | (a) the power may be exercised as occasion requires; and
-- src:488 | (b) the power includes—
-- src:489 | (i) power to remove or suspend, at any time, a person appointed to the office; and
-- src:490 | (ii) power to appoint another person to act in the office if a person appointed to the office is removed or suspended; and
-- src:491 | (iii) power to reinstate or reappoint a person removed or suspended; and
-- src:492 | (iv) power to appoint a person to act in the office if it is vacant (whether or not the office has ever been filled); and
-- src:493 | (v) power to appoint a person to act in the office if the person appointed to the office is absent or is unable to discharge the functions of the office (whether because of illness or otherwise); and
@ref s 25(1) (src:486-493)
GIVEN `an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `Power included in a power of appointment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power of appointment includes the power (s 25(1)(b))` IS
    IF NOT `an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER power
        WHEN `any other power` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:486 | (1) If an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office—
-- src:487 | (a) the power may be exercised as occasion requires; and
@ref s 25(1) (src:486-487)
GIVEN `an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power of appointment may be exercised as occasion requires (s 25(1)(a))` IS
    IF `an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:494 | (c) the power also includes power to reappoint a person to the office if the person is eligible to be appointed to the office.
@ref s 25(1) (src:494-494)
GIVEN `an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is eligible to be appointed to the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power of appointment also includes power to reappoint the person to the office (s 25(1)(c))` IS
    IF `an Act authorises or requires a person or body to appoint a person to an office` AND `the person is eligible to be appointed to the office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:495 | (2) The power to remove or suspend a person under subsection (1)(b) may be exercised even if the Act under which the person was appointed provides that the holder of the office to which the person was appointed is to hold office for a specified period.
@ref s 25(2) (src:495-495)
GIVEN `the Act under which the person was appointed provides that the holder of the office is to hold office for a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power to remove or suspend a person under s 25(1)(b) may be exercised (s 25(2))` IS JUST TRUE

-- src:496 | (3) The power to make an appointment under subsection (1)(b) may be exercised as occasion requires.
@ref s 25(3) (src:496-496)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power to make an appointment under s 25(1)(b) may be exercised as occasion requires (s 25(3))` IS JUST TRUE

-- src:497 | (4) An appointment under subsection (1)(b) may be expressed to have effect only in the circumstances specified in the instrument of appointment.
@ref s 25(4) (src:497-497)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appointment under s 25(1)(b) may be expressed to have effect only in the circumstances specified in the instrument of appointment (s 25(4))` IS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 26 and 27 -- appointment not affected by defect, hearing power`

DECLARE `Kind of appointment` IS ONE OF
    `an appointment to an office`
    `an appointment to act in an office`
    `an appointment to exercise a power`
    `an appointment to do anything else`

-- src:499 | The appointment of a person to an office, to act in an office, to exercise a power or to do anything else is not invalid merely because of a defect or irregularity in relation to the appointment.
@ref s 26 (src:499-499)
GIVEN appointment IS A `Kind of appointment`
      `there is a defect or irregularity in relation to the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment is invalid merely because of a defect or irregularity in relation to the appointment (s 26)` IS
    IF `there is a defect or irregularity in relation to the appointment` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Authority of a person or body conducting a hearing` IS ONE OF
    `to receive evidence`
    `to examine witnesses, and to administer oaths to witnesses, who have been lawfully called before the person or body`
    `anything else`

-- src:501 | A person or body authorised by law, or by consent of parties, to conduct a hearing for the purpose of the determination (by that or another person or body) of any matter has authority—
-- src:502 | (a) to receive evidence; and
-- src:503 | (b) to examine witnesses, and to administer oaths to witnesses, who have been lawfully called before the person or body.
@ref s 27 (src:501-503)
GIVEN `the person or body is authorised by law, or by consent of parties, to conduct a hearing for the purpose of the determination (by that or another person or body) of any matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      authority IS AN `Authority of a person or body conducting a hearing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person or body has authority (s 27)` IS
    IF NOT `the person or body is authorised by law, or by consent of parties, to conduct a hearing for the purpose of the determination (by that or another person or body) of any matter`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER authority
        WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 27A -- Delegation of functions or powers`

DECLARE `Way of delegating` IS ONE OF
    `to a person or body by name`
    `to a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office, by reference to the title of the office concerned`
    `in another way`

-- src:505 | (1) If an Act authorises a person or body to delegate a function or power, the person or body may, in accordance with the Act and any other applicable law, delegate the function or power to—
-- src:506 | (a) a person or body by name; or
-- src:507 | (b) a specified officer, or the holder of a specified office, by reference to the title of the office concerned.
@ref s 27A(1) (src:505-507)
GIVEN `an Act authorises a person or body to delegate a function or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `Way of delegating`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person or body may, in accordance with the Act and any other applicable law, delegate the function or power in the way (s 27A(1))` IS
    IF NOT `an Act authorises a person or body to delegate a function or power`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER way
        WHEN `in another way` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Form of delegation` IS ONE OF
    `general`
    `limited`
    `made from time to time`
    `revoked, wholly or partly, by the delegator`
    `any other form`

-- src:508 | (2) The delegation may be—
-- src:509 | (a) general or limited; and
-- src:510 | (b) made from time to time; and
-- src:511 | (c) revoked, wholly or partly, by the delegator.
@ref s 27A(2) (src:508-511)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of delegation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the delegation may be of the form (s 27A(2))` IS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `any other form` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:512 | (3) The delegation, or a revocation of the delegation, must be in, or evidenced by, writing signed by the delegator or, if the delegator is a body, by a person authorised by the body for the purpose.
@ref s 27A(3) (src:512-512)
GIVEN `the delegation, or a revocation of it, is in or evidenced by writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegator is a body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is signed by the delegator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is signed by a person authorised by the body for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requirement for writing and signature is met (s 27A(3))` IS
    JUST (   `the delegation, or a revocation of it, is in or evidenced by writing`
         AND (IF `the delegator is a body` THEN `the writing is signed by a person authorised by the body for the purpose` ELSE `the writing is signed by the delegator`))

-- src:513 | (3A) If the delegator is a body, the delegation may be made or revoked by a resolution of the body.
@ref s 27A(3A) (src:513-513)
GIVEN `the delegator is a body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the delegation may be made or revoked by a resolution of the body (s 27A(3A))` IS
    IF `the delegator is a body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- (3B): conditions and preliminary steps are presumed satisfied unless the contrary is established.
-- FORK once the contrary is established: NOTHING (the presumption is displaced) || JUST FALSE
-- src:514 | (3B) All conditions and preliminary steps required for the exercise of a delegation are presumed to have been satisfied and performed unless the contrary is established.
@ref s 27A(3B) (src:514-514)
GIVEN `the contrary is established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `all conditions and preliminary steps required for the exercise of a delegation are presumed to have been satisfied and performed (s 27A(3B))` IS
    IF `the contrary is established` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:515 | (3C) Laws apply to the delegate, and to other persons in relationship to the delegate, in the performance of the delegated function or in the exercise of a delegated power as if the delegate were the delegator.
@ref s 27A(3C) (src:515-515)
GIVEN `the function is performed or the power is exercised by a delegate under a delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `laws apply to the delegate, and to other persons in relationship to the delegate, as if the delegate were the delegator (s 27A(3C))` IS
    IF `the function is performed or the power is exercised by a delegate under a delegation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:516 | (3D) Anything done by or in relation to the delegate in relation to the delegation is taken to have been done by or in relation to the delegator.
@ref s 27A(3D) (src:516-516)
GIVEN `the thing is done by or in relation to the delegate in relation to the delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is taken to have been done by or in relation to the delegator (s 27A(3D))` IS
    IF `the thing is done by or in relation to the delegate in relation to the delegation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:519 | (4) A delegated function or power may be exercised only in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject.
@ref s 27A(4) (src:519-519)
GIVEN `the delegated function or power is exercised in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a delegated function or power may be exercised (s 27A(4))` IS
    IF `the delegated function or power is exercised in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:520 | (5) The delegate may, in the performance of a delegated function or in the exercise of a delegated power, do anything that is incidental to the delegated function or power.
@ref s 27A(5) (src:520-520)
GIVEN `the thing is incidental to the delegated function or power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the delegate may do the thing in the performance of the delegated function or the exercise of the delegated power (s 27A(5))` IS
    IF `the thing is incidental to the delegated function or power` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:521 | (6) A delegated function or power that purports to have been performed or exercised by the delegate is taken to have been properly performed or exercised by the delegate unless the contrary is proved.
@ref s 27A(6) (src:521-521)
GIVEN `the delegated function or power purports to have been performed or exercised by the delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the delegated function or power is taken to have been properly performed or exercised by the delegate (s 27A(6))` IS
    IF `the delegated function or power purports to have been performed or exercised by the delegate` AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:522 | (7) A delegated function or power that is properly performed or exercised by the delegate is taken to have been performed or exercised by the delegator.
@ref s 27A(7) (src:522-522)
GIVEN `the delegated function or power is properly performed or exercised by the delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the delegated function or power is taken to have been performed or exercised by the delegator (s 27A(7))` IS
    IF `the delegated function or power is properly performed or exercised by the delegate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:523 | (8) If, when performed or exercised by the delegator, a function or power is dependent on the delegator’s opinion, belief or state of mind, then, when performed or exercised by the delegate, the function or power is dependent on the delegate’s opinion, belief or state of mind.
@ref s 27A(8) (src:523-523)
GIVEN `the function or power, when performed or exercised by the delegator, is dependent on the delegator's opinion, belief or state of mind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function or power is performed or exercised by the delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the function or power is dependent on the delegate's opinion, belief or state of mind (s 27A(8))` IS
    IF `the function or power, when performed or exercised by the delegator, is dependent on the delegator's opinion, belief or state of mind` AND `the function or power is performed or exercised by the delegate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:524 | (8A) If—
-- src:525 | (a) the delegator is a specified officer or the holder of a specified office; and
-- src:526 | (b) the person who was the specified officer or holder of the specified office when the delegation was made ceases to be the officer or holder of the office;
-- src:527 | then—
-- src:528 | (c) the delegation continues in force; and
-- src:529 | (d) the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned is taken to be the delegator for the purposes of this section.
