    IF `the function or power is delegated to a specified officer or the holder of a specified office` AND `the person who was the specified officer or holder when the function or power was delegated ceases to be the officer or holder of the office`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:538 | (b) the function or power may be performed or exercised by the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned.
@ref s 27A(9) (src:538-538)
GIVEN `the function or power is delegated to a specified officer or the holder of a specified office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may perform the function or exercise the power (s 27A(9)(b))` IS
    IF `the function or power is delegated to a specified officer or the holder of a specified office` AND `the person is the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:539 | (10) A function or power that has been delegated may, despite the delegation, be performed or exercised by the delegator.
@ref s 27A(10) (src:539-539)
GIVEN `the function or power has been delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
