    IF `the function or power has been delegated` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:540 | (10A) The delegation of a function or power does not relieve the delegator of the delegator’s obligation to ensure that the function or power is properly performed or exercised.
@ref s 27A(10A) (src:540-540)
GIVEN `the function or power has been delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the delegation relieves the delegator of the delegator's obligation to ensure that the function or power is properly performed or exercised (s 27A(10A))` IS
    IF `the function or power has been delegated` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:541 | (11) Subject to subsection (12), this section applies to a subdelegation of a function or power in the same way as it applies to a delegation of a function or power.
@ref s 27A(11) (src:541-541)
GIVEN `the function or power is subdelegated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27A applies to the subdelegation in the same way as it applies to a delegation (s 27A(11))` IS
    IF `the function or power is subdelegated` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:542 | (12) If an Act authorises the delegation of a function or power, the function or power may be subdelegated only if the Act expressly authorises the function or power to be subdelegated.
@ref s 27A(12) (src:542-542)
GIVEN `an Act authorises the delegation of a function or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act expressly authorises the function or power to be subdelegated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the function or power may be subdelegated (s 27A(12))` IS
    IF NOT `an Act authorises the delegation of a function or power`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the Act expressly authorises the function or power to be subdelegated`

-- src:543 | (13) Writing purporting to be, or to contain, a delegation, or the revocation of a delegation, is evidence of the delegation or revocation.
@ref s 27A(13) (src:543-543)
GIVEN `the writing purports to be, or to contain, a delegation, or the revocation of a delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the writing is evidence of the delegation or revocation (s 27A(13))` IS
    IF `the writing purports to be, or to contain, a delegation, or the revocation of a delegation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:544 | (14) A certificate signed by the delegator (or, if the delegator is a body, by a person authorised by the body for the purpose) stating anything in relation to a delegation is evidence of the thing.
@ref s 27A(14) (src:544-544)
GIVEN `the certificate is signed by the delegator (or, if the delegator is a body, by a person authorised by the body for the purpose)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states something in relation to a delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
