    IF `the certificate is signed by the delegator (or, if the delegator is a body, by a person authorised by the body for the purpose)` AND `the certificate states something in relation to a delegation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:545 | (15) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in subsection (14) is taken to be the certificate, and to have been properly given, unless the contrary is established.
