GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resolution is interpreted as operating to the full extent of, but not to exceed, the Legislative Assembly's constitutional powers, subject to the Act, and distributively (s 29(1))` IS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution of the Legislative Assembly, or a committee of the Legislative Assembly, made under an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:563 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if part of a resolution would, apart from this section, be interpreted as exceeding authority—
